"""
V599 — Self-Contained Goal-Directed Path-Prior Search

Experiment:
    Test whether explicit target-conditioned proof search beats generic BFS /
    depth heuristics on the 44.87 GB semantic graph.

Core policy:
    1. Build a compact target-conditioned relation prior.
    2. Search with a bounded beam, not unconstrained hypothesis explosion.
    3. Score edges by target relation, endpoint match, profile transition,
       target-object reachability, and path cost.
    4. Verify every returned proof against the graph.
    5. Keep SQLite access batched and bounded.
    6. Run policy/seed jobs through one global worker pool (default 20).

The graph database is READ-ONLY. Relation profiles and the verified-path prior are embedded; no previous-version files are required.
"""

